flowchart TB
  U[Guests and hosts<br/>Web browsers and mobile clients] --> DNS[DNS + TLS<br/>Global traffic routing]
  DNS --> CDN[CDN / Edge network<br/>Static assets, images, cache headers]
  CDN --> FE[Frontend hosting<br/>React SPA + SSR-ready web tier]
  FE --> WAF[WAF + API Gateway<br/>Rate limits, auth, request validation]

  subgraph Services[Horizontally scalable backend services]
    Listing[Listing service]
    Booking[Booking service<br/>Idempotency + concurrency control]
    User[Identity and profile service]
    Payment[Payment adapter]
    Review[Review service]
    Notify[Notification worker]
  end

  WAF --> Listing
  WAF --> Booking
  WAF --> User
  WAF --> Review
  Booking --> Payment
  Booking --> Events[(Event bus / queue)]
  Events --> Notify
  Events --> Indexer[Search indexer worker]

  subgraph Data[Durable storage and performance layer]
    SQL[(Primary relational database<br/>Multi-AZ, read replicas, backups)]
    Cache[(Redis cluster<br/>Sessions, hot listings, rate limits)]
    Blob[(Object storage<br/>Photos, documents, lifecycle rules)]
    Search[(Search cluster<br/>Geo, filters, availability facets)]
  end

  Listing --> SQL
  Booking --> SQL
  User --> SQL
  Review --> SQL
  Listing --> Cache
  Booking --> Cache
  Listing --> Blob
  CDN --> Blob
  Indexer --> Search
  WAF --> Search

  subgraph Delivery[Deployment and operations]
    Git[Git repository] --> CI[CI pipeline<br/>Tests, lint, security scan]
    CI --> Registry[Container / artifact registry]
    Registry --> Deploy[Blue-green or rolling deployment]
    Deploy --> FE
    Deploy --> Services
    Deploy --> Workers[Autoscaled workers]
    Services --> Obs[Logs, metrics, traces, alerts]
    FE --> Obs
  end

  classDef edge fill:#e8f1ff,stroke:#2563eb,color:#0f172a
  classDef service fill:#ecfdf5,stroke:#059669,color:#0f172a
  classDef data fill:#fff7ed,stroke:#ea580c,color:#0f172a
  classDef ops fill:#f5f3ff,stroke:#7c3aed,color:#0f172a
  class DNS,CDN,FE,WAF edge
  class Listing,Booking,User,Payment,Review,Notify,Indexer service
  class SQL,Cache,Blob,Search data
  class Git,CI,Registry,Deploy,Workers,Obs ops

  %% Scaling notes:
  %% - CDN and stateless frontend/backend instances scale horizontally.
  %% - Booking writes use transactions, idempotency keys, and row-level locks.
  %% - Read replicas and Redis absorb read traffic; object storage offloads media.
  %% - Search is eventually consistent and rebuilt from the event stream.
  %% - Multi-AZ backups, health checks, observability, and blue-green releases support resilience.
      
